    <statement><p>Let <m>W_1</m> be the solid half-cone bounded
by  <m>z=\sqrt{x^2+y^2}</m>, <m>z=4</m> and the
<m>yz</m>-plane with <m>x \le 0</m>, and let
Let <m>W_2</m> be the solid half-cone bounded
by  <m>z=\sqrt{x^2+y^2}</m>, <m>z=4</m> and the
<m>xz</m>-plane with <m>y \ge 0</m>.</p>
<p>For each of the following, decide (without calculating its value)
whether the integral is positive, negative, or zero.</p>
<p><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_1} x\,dV</m> is
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li><li>
<p>zero</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><alert>(b)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_1} x^2 y\,dV</m> is
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0002"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li><li>
<p>zero</p>
</li></ul></p>
<p><alert>(c)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_2} y z\,dV</m> is
<ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0003"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
<p>positive</p>
</li><li>
<p>negative</p>
</li><li>
<p>zero</p>
</li></ul></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{negative}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{zero}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{positive}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_1} x\,dV</m> is negative,



<alert>(b)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_1} x^2 y\,dV</m> is zero, and



<alert>(c)</alert>
<m>\int_{W_2} y z\,dV</m> is positive.



</solution>
